# /*****************************************************************************/
# * File: synth.ys
# * Author: Olavo Alves Barros Silva
# * Contact: olavo.barros@ufv.com
# * Date: 2026-07-23
# * Description: Yosys script for falin_cnn_top - coarse area/cell-count
# * check, not a full technology-mapped synthesis. Run with:
# *   cd src/hw/cnn && yosys synth.ys
# *
# * Same rationale as src/hw/gaf_encoder/synth.ys: stops before
# * `techmap`/`abc`. This design has several large ROMs (classifier weight:
# * 7*128=896 entries, conv3 weight: 128*32*9=36864 entries) plus the
# * conv/pool/GAP module hierarchies - full gate-level optimization would be
# * even slower here than for the GAF encoder. `stat` right after
# * `memory_collect` reports raw cell counts ($mul, $mem, etc.) without
# * expanding them. Real technology-mapped synthesis (LUTs/FFs/DSPs/BRAMs on
# * the actual xc7z020) is Vivado's job later (Task 8 of
# * misc/docs/fpga_implementation_plan.md), not Yosys's here.
# /*****************************************************************************/

read_verilog -sv conv_bn_relu_layer.v
read_verilog -sv maxpool2x2.v
read_verilog -sv global_avg_pool.v
read_verilog -sv classifier.v
read_verilog -sv falin_cnn_top.v
hierarchy -check -top falin_cnn_top

proc
opt
memory_collect

tee -o area_report.json stat -json
stat

# --- Further steps (commented out - only if a real gate-level estimate is
# needed later; expect this to be considerably slower than the GAF encoder) ---
# synth -flatten
# write_blif -gates falin_cnn_top.blif
# abc -liberty <path-to-cell-library>.lib
# stat
